<section aria-label="RPG Maker MZ save editing guide" class="not-prose mt-14 space-y-12">
  <!-- Intro Summary Card -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">What is an .rmmzsave editor?</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        An <strong>.rmmzsave editor</strong> opens a compatible RPG Maker MZ save slot, displays its stored values, and
        rebuilds the file after an edit. SaveFileTool runs online while keeping save contents on your device: select the
        numbered slot above, review the detected money value, and download your edited copy bundled with its original
        backup. No account or software installation is required.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
        MZ saves can hold currency, actor data, equipment, event flags, and map state. Start with the <strong>gold or
        money field</strong>, which is the tested editing workflow. A game may label that currency as Gems, coins, or
        another name in its menu—compare the detected amount with your in-game menu before editing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Save Folder Location with Visual Diagram -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50/70 dark:bg-gray-800/50 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Where to find RPG Maker MZ save files</h2>
    <figure class="my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-sm">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/save-folder-location.jpg" width="1376" height="768"
        alt="Desktop folder tree showing RPG Maker MZ save/file1.rmmzsave and RPG Maker MV www/save/file1.rpgsave locations"
        class="block h-auto w-full"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
        Choose a numbered manual slot such as <code>file1.rmmzsave</code> inside <code>save/</code>—skip <code>config.rmmzsave</code> and <code>global.rmmzsave</code>.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">Desktop Installation</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Open the <code>save/</code> folder</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          In most desktop MZ games, numbered saves live in <code>save/</code> beneath the installation folder (not next
          to a desktop shortcut). Create a fresh save and match its modification timestamp to confirm the active folder.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-600">Manual vs Autosave</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Pick a numbered manual slot</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Avoid <code>config.rmmzsave</code> and <code>global.rmmzsave</code>. MZ also uses slot 0 for autosave; a
          manual numbered slot like <code>file1.rmmzsave</code> is easier to identify and test safely.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 p-5">
        <div class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-600">Browser-Hosted MZ Games</div>
        <h3 class="mt-1 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Stored in IndexedDB</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Web-hosted MZ games usually store progress in IndexedDB rather than writing an <code>.rmmzsave</code> file to
          disk. Use the game's own export feature if provided; this picker requires an actual <code>.rmmzsave</code> file.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Step-by-Step Workflow with Visual Diagram -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Edit MZ money with a controlled backup workflow</h2>
    <figure class="my-6 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-gray-800 shadow-sm">
      <img
        src="/images/guides/safe-edit-workflow.jpg" width="1376" height="768"
        alt="Four-step safe RPG Maker MZ save editing workflow: backup original, edit money locally, extract ZIP, and verify in game"
        class="block h-auto w-full"
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-800/90 px-4 py-2.5 text-center text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
        Controlled backup-first flow: keep your untouched original until the rebuilt MZ slot loads cleanly in game.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ol class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">1</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Note currency &amp; exit</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Check your currency in the game menu, save manually, exit the game, and copy the slot to a backup folder.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">2</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Confirm &amp; edit money</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Select the file above, verify the detected amount matches, and change only money on your first test.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-blue-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">3</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Extract &amp; replace slot</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Unzip the download and place the rebuilt numbered file into <code>save/</code>—not the zip or backup-prefixed copy.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="rounded-xl border border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 p-4">
        <span class="inline-flex h-7 w-7 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-emerald-600 text-xs font-bold text-white">4</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">Restart &amp; verify</h3>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">Load the slot, check currency, party, and location, and keep your backup as a recovery point.</p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>

  <!-- Real Game Verification Highlight -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-emerald-200 dark:border-emerald-800/70 bg-emerald-50/70 dark:bg-emerald-950/40 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
      <span class="rounded-full bg-emerald-600 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-white">Real MZ Game Test</span>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-emerald-950 dark:text-emerald-200">A real MZ game test: Gems in Haven</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-100">
        Our recorded MZ verification used a real desktop save from <strong>Haven: Secret of Caledria</strong>. After
        editing its money value and restarting the game, the menu displayed <strong>Gems 999,999</strong> at
        <strong>Olund Fort</strong> (the in-game location). Separate regression checks also verify byte-for-byte
        original backup preservation and clean gold-only rebuilds.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-100">
        This confirms the tested money workflow in that game save, but does not guarantee every Haven feature, MZ
        release, or custom plugin setup. Actor levels, inventory, variables, and switches remain candidate edits—always
        use your game's own loading behavior as the final check.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- MZ vs MV Comparison Table -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">MZ .rmmzsave and MV .rpgsave are different formats</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
      Use this RPG Maker MZ save editor online for actual <code>.rmmzsave</code> files. Renaming an MV file to
      <code>.rmmzsave</code> does not convert its compression. Older RPG Maker formats, executables, and project
      archives are outside this page's accepted inputs.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900/60 text-xs uppercase tracking-wide text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300 dark:text-gray-300">
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Engine</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Extension</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Standard Compression</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Typical Save Path</th>
            <th class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold">Editor</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-100 dark:divide-gray-700">
          <tr class="bg-blue-50/40 dark:bg-blue-950/30">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MZ</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>.rmmzsave</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">pako (zlib/deflate)</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>save/</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">Current page</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MV</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>.rpgsave</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">LZString + Base64</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3"><code>www/save/</code> or <code>save/</code></td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3">
              <a href="/editor/rpg-maker-mv/" class="font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 hover:underline">Open MV Save Editor &rarr;</a>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Plugins & Privacy Two-Column Cards -->
  <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 dark:border-amber-800/70 bg-amber-50/60 dark:bg-amber-950/40 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-950 dark:text-amber-200">Why plugins and custom saves may not work</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100">
        Developers can alter MZ's save process with plugins—changing where files are written, which objects are stored,
        whether contents are encrypted, or using a custom currency instead of the engine's standard money field.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-100">
        If a file is rejected or fails to load after editing, confirm its extension, restore your backup, and try a
        smaller money-only change on a fresh manual slot rather than editing unknown fields.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-slate-50 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Privacy, backups, and the 10 MB limit</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        Your selected save is read and rebuilt locally in the browser—nothing is sent to a server. Optional local
        history stays in browser storage on your device and is separate from your manual disk backups.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-gray-300">
        The file limit is <strong>10 MB</strong>. Choose the individual <code>.rmmzsave</code> file rather than a whole
        project or zip archive, and never delete arbitrary sections of a large plugin save just to fit the limit.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Collapsible FAQ Accordion -->
  <div class="rounded-2xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-white dark:bg-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 p-6 shadow-sm sm:p-8">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">RPG Maker MZ save editing questions</h2>
    <div class="mt-5 space-y-3">
      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Why does my game call the money Gems instead of gold?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Developers can customize the displayed currency name. In the Haven test, the menu label was Gems while the
          edited value was the party's money field. Compare the detected amount with your game's menu—if they differ,
          the game may use a separate custom currency system.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Should I edit the autosave or a manual slot?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Start with a manual slot you can select explicitly on the load screen. An autosave can be overwritten as you
          continue playing or enter a new area, making it harder to verify whether your edit loaded cleanly.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Why did the downloaded save appear not to change anything?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Confirm the active installation, slot filename, and directory. Extract the zip before copying the edited file
          and restart the game before loading. A running game or cloud sync can overwrite disk files with an older copy.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>Does Folder Mode make inventory or quest edits verified?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Folder Mode reads names from the game's JSON data files to help recognize actor, item, variable, and switch
          IDs, but labels provide context rather than a compatibility guarantee. Test candidate fields individually in
          a spare slot first.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group rounded-xl border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 bg-gray-50/70 dark:bg-gray-900/50 open:bg-white dark:open:bg-gray-800">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between p-4 font-semibold text-gray-900 dark:text-white">
          <h3>How do I recover from a save that will not load?</h3>
          <span class="ml-4 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 transition-transform group-open:rotate-180">&#9662;</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="px-4 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-300">
          Exit the game and replace the edited numbered file with your original backup under the expected slot name.
          Verify that the restored slot loads before retrying, and keep any failed export separate from your working
          backup.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
